Z||000016||Slammed Fiero||10-18-2001||04:30 PM||||Just to throw in a little bit of info..<P>A guy in our club is into Ferrari's. He has a 308 , a Dino and something else (Can't remember , 4 seater , early 60's car) <P>In anycase he had to get the motor on the 308 Rebuilt. It's a pre 84 car so it is not Quatrovaloe (sp jay?) His car is a 77 I believe , an import not originally destined to North America. It has webbers, also a desirable fiberglass bodied car<P>$17,500 later he had his new motor ..pushing the car to 60mph in a little under 7 sec.<P>There really apples and organes. The cars weren't built for Light to light , low end grunt. But high speed touring. I have had a chance to ride in a 308 , a Testarossa and a 348 Spyder. Very progressive power. Very high maintenance costs. But there expected as with any car that is theleast bit exotic. A tune up on a twin plug 3.8 ltr 911 motr can run 2 grand , just for scheduled maintenance<P>Although a 308 GT4 seems common as a daily driver among Ferrari enthuasists.. Cheap too.<BR>I just want the sound!<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Archie||10-18-2001||04:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>hey archie im not busting on your replica one bit. you got one h*ll of an operation goin on. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No problem at all.<P>The body that is on the Black car came from molds that were actually taken off of a real F-40 (I'm positive of that). The Fiero chassis was stretched and chopped to fit under the body.<P>That is why it looks real. It wasn't a body made to fit a Fiero chassis, it was a Fiero Chassis made to fit the body.<P>Archie<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Jay||10-18-2001||06:14 PM||||Quatrovalvole or as we say QV.<BR>The 308GT4 is basically a 308 2 valve car that was designed by Bertone instead of the 308 designed by Pininfarina.  Not many like the look of the GT4 hence it is cheaper.  I think the closest replica to the real thing is the 308/328.  The only thing that gives it away is the roof line and the interior.<P>Archie you're right nobody would by a kit that had bare floors and no creature comforts.  But they would spend a quarter of a million on the real F40.<P>The F50 on the other hand had all the creature comforts and a formula one engine and can be had for half a million.  Where do I sign? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||rogergarrison||10-18-2001||08:03 PM||||Arch, I didnt dislike yours. the chopped top def made it look a lot better. Thats the problem with the GT40 replicas too, needs a chop top to look anywhere close.||||reg||1
Z||000020||artherd||10-18-2001||11:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<P>I just want the sound!<P>JM <BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You and me both!!!<P>My god, once you've driven a F355, you will never, ever, go back!!! (that was one of the best nights of my life  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
